.TH TOUCH 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
touch \- make empty files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B touch
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B touch
makes each
.I file
that doesn't exist yet, empty. A file that exists already is left as it is.
A file that can't be made is reported on standard error as
.BI "touch: " reason
and the rest are still tried.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every file exists afterwards, 1 if any could not be made.
.SH NOTES
Unlike GNU touch, it never changes the times of a file that exists (there
is no call to set them), and it has no options
.RB ( \-a ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-d ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR rm (1)
